## Open Questions (decide before starting)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which clinical sub-domain to focus on?**
> The PDFs strongly recommend scoping to ONE domain (e.g., infectious disease, primary care triage). Trying to cover all of medicine will hurt retrieval precision. This choice affects everything — corpus filtering, evaluation queries, paper framing.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which LLM will you use for the real mode?**
> Current code defaults to the mock reasoner. For paper results you need either a GPT-4/Claude API key or a local open-source model (Meditron, BioMistral). Which do you have access to?

> [!WARNING]
> **RAGAS requires an LLM-as-judge internally** (it calls an LLM to score faithfulness). This costs API tokens. Budget this before wiring it in.

> [!NOTE]
> **PostgreSQL is optional for a research prototype.** SQLite for query logs + ChromaDB for vectors is a perfectly valid research stack. Don't let the DB setup become a time sink.
